        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="PON01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Ponsonby</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1755-03-05">
                        <placeName>Ireland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1817-07-08"/>
                    <occupation>lord chancellor of Ireland</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin records his death.  Also there seem to be meetings at <persName key="CUR01">Curran's</persName> in 1799
      and a call on him by Godwin in the August of 1800 when Godwin is in Ireland.
    Ponsonby defended suspected rebels after the 1798 rising and fears of a legislative
    union prompted his return to the House of Commons as MP for Galway in 1798, where he fought hard
    against the bill for Union. </p>
                        <p>There is one entry to Ponsoby in 1826, some years after his death, which is uncoded, but may be a relative.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
